{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794391145,"nonce":"GrKbFcURqoKMbINyreZcHqrAnbE=","title":"Plan: move time- and scroll-driven visual work to the GPU, with the CPU keeping the settled state","message":"Phases: 07f1e4b (P0), 1243275 (P1), 122c606 (P2), 29e250d (P3), 04efbde (P4), 54771c4 (P5), 5092663 (P6), c2c4531 (P7).\n\nSource: the owner's survey of UI features that can be deferred to the GPU, checked against the code by four read-only surveys (animation and motion, render pipeline, scroll and hit testing, public API). Nothing here is measured yet; P0 does that first.\n\n\nThe survey asked whether animation runs CPU-side and re-collects primitives. The answer is mixed, and the existing mechanism is the starting point.\n- There is already a fast path. Motion bindings (`apply_binding_deltas`) and CSS animations (`apply_css_deltas`) patch fields of primitives in cached batches, and promoted subtrees are baked to textures and blitted with live translate, scale and opacity (rotate z for motion). Only opacity, 2D translate and scale are composite-promotable.\n- But the CPU still evaluates every animated value every frame, patches, and re-uploads the whole dynamic batch (`write_primitives_safe`; `write_primitives_partial` has no callers). Animations fall back to a full tree walk plus a second walk to collect text, SVG and images whenever text, SVG or an image sits in the animated subtree, for `motion()` enter and exit, FLIP, `animate_bounds`, non-promotable CSS, and for every scroll frame.\n- `GpuPrimitive` is 34 vec4 (544 B) with no node id, no opacity, no time. Transforms are flattened on the CPU at emit. The only SDF uniform is `viewport_size`.\n- Hit testing, accessibility and focus read settled layout position plus scroll, never the animated transform. So animating visuals only on the GPU does not change those consumers.\n- Springs are integrated per tick with RK4. At least six time bases exist, all dt-integrated with caps.\n- Scroll is a paint-time translation baked into primitives, implemented four times (paint, collection, hit test, `get_absolute_bounds`).\n- A resize replaces the whole tree and reallocates the static layer.\n- The A14 is fill-bound at about 2.5 ns per fragment (36c7812). Moving work to the GPU must go through the vertex stage or a per-instance value, never extra per-fragment work.\n\n\nDefer when the input is a small parameter or time, the output is pixels, and the CPU never needs to read the result. Keep on the CPU anything structural (layout, text shaping), semantic (hit testing, accessibility, focus) or that feeds application state.\n\n\n| # | Candidate | Today | Phase |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Transform and opacity animation: CSS transform, opacity, `motion()` bindings, FLIP, visual-only `animate_bounds` | CPU eval per frame, batch patch, full re-upload, full-walk fallback with text inside | P1, P2 |\n| 2 | Time-only effects and the idle loop: spinners, skeleton, caret blink, flow shaders, ripples | the whole frame path runs per frame (59d424e) | P3 |\n| 3 | Scroll translation, sticky and fixed, scroll-linked effects | full walk every scroll frame, four copies of the math | P4 |\n| 4 | Colour, border, radius, shadow, filter parameter animation | value-matching CPU patcher, stale fields | P5 |\n| 5 | Layer effect parameters (blur radius, colour matrix, drop shadow, glow) | pass count changes with radius, one submit per effect | P5 |\n| 6 | Resize stretch | tree replaced, layer reallocated, nothing to show meanwhile (4f48675) | P6 |\n| 7 | Snapshot transitions (page, shared element) | not supported | P6 |\n\n\n- Layout and reflow, and any animation of width, height, padding, margin, gap, flex or inset. These re-run `compute_layout` each frame today; authors who want cheap motion animate transform (FLIP). No automatic conversion: stretching text changes the look.\n- Text shaping and line breaking; glyph quads are rebuilt on full paints.\n- Hit testing (retained tree, settled bounds; an ID buffer needs readback), accessibility tree, focus and IME geometry.\n- App-visible values: `AnimatedValue::get`, `ScrollRef`, `watch_y`, `MotionHandle::progress`. They stay correct by evaluating the CPU mirror on demand (P1).\n- Vector path rasterisation on the GPU (Vello-style): large, and not where the CPU time goes.\n- A depth buffer for z-order: all 2D passes run without depth, draw order is painter's order, and the mobile fill cost points at blending and discard, not sorting. Revisit only with a measurement.\n- Compute culling and indirect draws: virtual lists and the scroll overscan band already bound the work. Revisit after P4.\n\n\n1. **Settled pose plus a delta.** Primitives are emitted at their final pose. An animated node has a row in a GPU node table holding a delta (translate, scale about an origin, rotate z, opacity multiplier) and a parent slot. The cached batch stays valid for the whole animation, and the CPU never has to know an in-between value to be correct.\n2. **Descriptors.** `{ start_ms, duration_ms, from, to, curve, initial_velocity }` with curves linear, cubic-bezier, steps and closed-form spring. Evaluated against one frame clock. The CPU holds the same descriptor and the same maths for read-back; retargeting evaluates the current value and velocity on the CPU and writes a new descriptor.\n3. **Two steps for the table.** First the CPU writes evaluated rows for animated nodes only; then rows hold descriptors and the vertex stage evaluates them. The second step is what gives zero per-frame CPU.\n4. **Sparse.** Static nodes use slot 0 (identity). Cost is paid only by nodes that animate.\n5. **Tiers.** Tier 0 (storage buffer) and tier 2 (data texture) get the table. Tier 1 keeps today's CPU patcher as the fallback behind a capability flag. Deep chains (more than four animated ancestors) also fall back.\n6. **Wake scheduling.** The app sleeps until the next descriptor end or timer; clock-only frames skip tick, rebuild and walk.\n7. **Scroll** reuses the same table: the CPU physics writes one offset per container; the batch carries an overscan band; momentum can become a descriptor with lazy read-back.\n\n\nCSS is the public surface; the GPU work mostly appears as existing CSS getting cheaper.\n- Added, all web standards: `steps()`, `linear()`, `animation-play-state`, individual `translate`/`scale`/`rotate`, `animation-timeline: scroll()|view()`, `will-change`, `prefers-reduced-motion`, `view-transition-name` and the view-transition pseudo-elements.\n- blinc_animation (additive): `Curve`, `AnimationDescriptor`, `Easing::to_curve`, `Spring::to_descriptor`, `AnimatedValue::descriptor`.\n- blinc_gpu: `GpuPrimitive` gains a node-slot field; `NodeTable` and renderer entry points. Breaking for struct literals; construct through builders.\n- Deprecated then removed: per-call duration builders (`Motion::fade_in(ms)` and siblings, `AnimationPreset::*(ms)`, `AnimationBuilder::with_duration`, `VisualAnimationConfig::timed`); `Div::animate_layout` (deprecated since 0.3.0).\n- Kept, documented as CPU-driven app state: `AnimatedValue`, `Div::animate`, `Motion::translate_x/y/scale/rotate/opacity(SharedAnimatedValue)`, `register_tick_callback`.\n- Semver: one breaking release (0.7.0) adds `#[non_exhaustive]` to `RenderProps`, `KeyframeProperties`, `MotionBindings`, `ElementStyle` and the other animation-facing structs. None has it today, so every field added so far has been a breaking change.\n- Read-back APIs keep their signatures and meaning: `AnimatedValue::get`, `Spring::value`, `AnimatedTimeline::get`, `use_spring`, `MotionBindings::get_*`, `MotionHandle::progress`, `ScrollRef::*`.\n- Sibling repo blinc_abi: matches `PropertyId` by literal id and uses `PartialPropertyUpdate` and `RenderProps` directly; changes to those move in step with it. Descriptors are plain data and are the natural form for 36603e0.\n\n\n- Animations use absolute time, so a stalled frame skips ahead instead of pausing (CSS behaviour; today dt is capped).\n- Spring settling follows the closed form, not RK4 with absolute epsilons; values differ slightly.\n- Reduced motion becomes honoured.\n\n\n- Mobile fill cost: no per-fragment table fetch; opacity and tracks arrive as flat varyings; measure the A14 before P5.\n- Three data tiers, each needing the new lane (struct, russl Primitive, tier-2 loader, tier-1 vertex attributes, parity tests, about fifteen struct literals).\n- Windows FXC and other shader portability rules (see P2); the HLSL test must stay green.\n- CPU and shader maths must agree: shared test vectors (P1), old-versus-new pixel tests per phase.\n- Culling versus GPU scroll: the batch is only correct inside the emitted band (P4).\n- Duplicated scroll math drifting while 4a is not done.\n\n\n1. Time semantics (skip on stall) and closed-form springs: accept the visible changes?\n2. Tier 1: keep the CPU patcher forever, or require a vertex texture fetch?\n3. Which non-standard CSS properties (`rotate-x`, `translate-z`, `depth`, `light-*`, `glass-*`) are accepted domain extras?\n4. Should russl grow a CPU target so the curve maths has one source?\n5. 0.7.0 as the single breaking release, or earlier for `#[non_exhaustive]` alone?\n\n\n`cursor_inside_last_leaf` staleness and missing hover refresh after scroll; whether `update_scroll_content_dimensions` re-clamps on shrink; whether the settled streak is double-counted in `compute_animation_status`; how scheduler-thread and UI-thread ticking of the CSS store are reconciled; how often real CSS animations land in the background batch; whether `apply_binding_deltas` leaves clip, gradient, shadow and border stale; exact flatten-versus-group split for opacity.\n\n\n3ffa360 (bound writes and transitions), 4f48675 (resize rebuilds the tree), 59d424e (flow shader keeps the CPU loop), 36c7812 (mobile fill-bound), 956e030 (mobile scroll frame rate), 3c7afb9 (damage rect), 36603e0 (one animation engine for the ABI), 44c33ff (scheduler dt cap), f3b2da2 (keyframes cannot move gradient stops), 1854094 (renderer rework candidates), 2c565dc (retire stateful closures), c546365 and fc977db (lean GPU stack: keep the table behind the narrow backend interface).","files":null}]}